---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contact | InfraOpsX"
  description="Contact InfraOpsX for Linux, Docker, Kubernetes, self-hosted deployment and infrastructure troubleshooting."
  lang="en"
  canonicalPath="/contact/"
  enPath="/contact/"
  zhPath="/zh/contact/"
>
  <Header locale="en" switchHref="/zh/contact/" />

  <main>
    <section class="contact-hero">
      <div class="container contact-hero-inner">
        <div>
          <span class="section-label">CONTACT</span>
          <h1>Need help with infrastructure?</h1>
          <p>
            If you are trying to deploy, migrate or troubleshoot a Linux,
            Docker or Kubernetes environment, email me with the context and
            symptoms. Clear technical information makes it much easier to
            understand the problem quickly.
          </p>
        </div>

        <aside class="contact-email-card">
          <span class="contact-card-label">BEST WAY TO REACH ME</span>
          <a class="contact-email" href="mailto:hello@oeax.de">
            hello@oeax.de
          </a>
          <p>
            For project inquiries, deployment work and infrastructure
            troubleshooting.
          </p>
          <a class="button primary contact-email-button" href="mailto:hello@oeax.de">
            Send an email
          </a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="contact-section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="contact-grid">
          <article class="contact-panel">
            <span class="contact-number">01</span>
            <h2>What I can help with</h2>
            <ul class="contact-list">
              <li>Linux services and infrastructure troubleshooting</li>
              <li>Docker / Docker Compose deployment and migration</li>
              <li>Self-hosted application deployment</li>
              <li>Kubernetes deployment and troubleshooting</li>
              <li>Nginx, reverse proxy and HTTPS configuration</li>
              <li>Prometheus / Grafana monitoring for servers, containers and infrastructure</li>
              <li>Storage, disk I/O and networking diagnostics</li>
            </ul>
          </article>

          <article class="contact-panel">
            <span class="contact-number">02</span>
            <h2>What to include in your message</h2>
            <ol class="contact-list">
              <li>What are you trying to deploy, migrate or fix?</li>
              <li>What environment are you using?</li>
              <li>What error, symptom or unexpected behavior are you seeing?</li>
              <li>What have you already tried?</li>
              <li>Is this a production environment or a test environment?</li>
            </ol>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="contact-example">
          <span class="section-label">GOOD FIRST MESSAGE</span>
          <pre><code>Subject: Kubernetes Pod scheduling issue

Environment:
- Kubernetes cluster
- 6 worker nodes
- Container runtime: containerd

Problem:
One workload remains Pending.

What I checked:
kubectl describe pod shows scheduler errors related to
affinity and CPU requests.

Goal:
Identify the actual scheduling blocker and the safest fix.</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="contact-safety">
          <h2>Before sending logs or configuration</h2>
          <p>
            Please remove passwords, API keys, tokens, private keys and other
            secrets. Hostnames, IP addresses and company-specific identifiers
            can also be anonymized when they are not needed for diagnosis.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="contact-bottom">
          <div>
            <span class="section-label">READY?</span>
            <h2>Tell me what you are working on.</h2>
          </div>
          <a class="button primary" href="mailto:hello@oeax.de">
            hello@oeax.de
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer locale="en" />
</BaseLayout>
